From aded90d9ca6b98b1631311ff2c10ae60ccf9dac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angel Krastev <akrastev@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:36:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mlpostprocess: yolov8 bug fix

Bug: class_idx was computed as idx / n_paxels, which is always 0
since idx < n_paxels so every detection was misclassified as
class 0. Box coordinates were read from bboxes[id + r*n_paxels],
where id is a flat index into the scores tensor
(shaped (1, num_classes, n_paxels)); reused against bboxes
(shaped (1, 4, n_paxels), no class dimension), this read
out-of-row (or out-of-bounds) data for any anchor whose
winning class wasn't 0, producing scrambled/oversized boxes.

Fix: derive class_idx from id (id / n_paxels) instead of idx, and
index bboxes by idx (the anchor position) instead of id.

Signed-off-by: Angel Krastev <akrastev@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Girish K <girik@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/qualcomm/qimsdk/commit/aded90d9ca6b98b1631311ff2c10ae60ccf9dac0]
---
 .../modules/object-detection/ml-postprocess-yolov8.cc  | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gstreamer/gst-plugin-mlpostprocess/modules/object-detection/ml-postprocess-yolov8.cc b/gstreamer/gst-plugin-mlpostprocess/modules/object-detection/ml-postprocess-yolov8.cc
index 32d8d35..f4ec60a 100644
--- a/gstreamer/gst-plugin-mlpostprocess/modules/object-detection/ml-postprocess-yolov8.cc
+++ b/gstreamer/gst-plugin-mlpostprocess/modules/object-detection/ml-postprocess-yolov8.cc
@@ -246,17 +246,17 @@ void Module::ParseDualblockFrame(const Tensors& tensors, Dictionary& mlparams,
     for (uint32_t num = (idx + n_paxels); num < (n_classes * n_paxels); num += n_paxels)
       id = (TensorCompareValues(scores, num, id) > 0) ? num : id;
 
-    uint32_t class_idx = idx / n_paxels;
+    uint32_t class_idx = id / n_paxels;
 
     double confidence = scores[id];
 
     if (confidence < threshold_)
       continue;
 
-    double cx = bboxes[id + 0 * n_paxels];
-    double cy = bboxes[id + 1 * n_paxels];
-    double w  = bboxes[id + 2 * n_paxels];
-    double h  = bboxes[id + 3 * n_paxels];
+    double cx = bboxes[idx + 0 * n_paxels];
+    double cy = bboxes[idx + 1 * n_paxels];
+    double w  = bboxes[idx + 2 * n_paxels];
+    double h  = bboxes[idx + 3 * n_paxels];
 
     LOG(logger_, kLog, "Class: %u Confidence: %.2f CX x CY[%f, %f] W x H: [%f, %f]",
         class_idx, confidence, cx, cy, w, h);
-- 
